Environment note (unrelated pre-existing issue, not caused by this change):
the local `~/.databrickscfg` `DEFAULT` CLI profile's OAuth session is
expired. Any code path that falls through to `WorkspaceClient()` default
auth (e.g. `back.core.databricks.get_local_user_email`, `RegistryCfg.from_domain`,
`DatabricksHelpers._resolve_registry_cfg`) now hits the SDK's slow
OAuth-refresh retry/backoff instead of failing fast, and because
`get_local_user_email` is `functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1)`-wrapped, the very
first test in a session to touch it stalls every later test that needs the
same cached call for minutes. This is environmental (fixed by
`databricks auth login --profile fe-vm-bcayla-demos`, which requires
interactive browser auth) and reproduces on a clean tree — it is not a
regression from this change. Full-suite run for this session used
`DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE=__nonexistent_profile_for_fast_fail__` (env-only,
no code change) to force those paths to fail fast instead of retrying:
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 4753 passed, 276 skipped,
5 deselected, 1 xfailed in 39.25s, 3 failures — all 3 confirmed to be
artifacts of that env override (they hang without it, and read
CLI-profile-derived config the override intentionally blanks), not real
regressions: `test_health.py::TestCheckDatabricksAuth::test_local_mode_with_cli_profile`,
`test_graph_engine_config.py::TestSettingsServiceGraphEngineConfig::test_get_graph_engine_config_result{,_empty}`.

Deploy: `make deploy` (target `dev-lakebase-07x`, profile `fe-vm-bcayla-demos`) →
bundle deployed, both apps started and verified `RUNNING`
(`ontobricks-07x`, `mcp-ontobricks-07x`); `/healthz` returned 200 on both at
deploy time and again ~60s later (no post-start crash).

## Add named Neo4j connection profiles

Context: Settings stored a single flat Neo4j Bolt profile, and Domain → KG
exposed an optional database override via SHOW DATABASES. Admins need
multiple named connections (URI, database, username, Databricks secret) and
must bind each Neo4j domain to one of them. Spec:
`documentation/superpowers/specs/2026-08-07-neo4j-named-connections-design.md`.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/graphdb/engine_config.py`
   Add `list_neo4j_connections` / `resolve_neo4j_connection`; finalize
   `neo4j.connections[]`; no auto-migration from flat uri/username.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`
   Resolve `domain.info.neo4j_connection` to a named profile for Neo4jStore.
3. `src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py` / `Domain.py`
   Persist required `neo4j_connection`; retire domain `neo4j_database` write.
4. `src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py` / `src/api/routers/internal/settings.py`
   List connections API; save `connections[]` with password strip +
   referential delete/rename guard; Test/Objects/Health take `connection_name`.
5. `src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py` / `lakebase/store.py`
   Include `neo4j_connection` on domain metadata for referential scans.
6. `src/front/templates/settings.html` / `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`
   Master–detail Connections UI (add/edit/delete); Objects/Health use selection.
7. `src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html` /
   `domain-information.js` / `domain.js`
   Required Neo4j Connection dropdown lists Settings connection names.
8. Tests under `tests/units/graphdb/`, `tests/units/settings/`, `tests/units/domain/`
   Updated for connections[] and neo4j_connection.
9. `documentation/superpowers/specs/2026-08-07-neo4j-named-connections-design.md`
   / `documentation/superpowers/plans/2026-08-07-neo4j-named-connections.md`
   Design + implementation plan.

