## Fix Domain Neo4j connection picker population and save

Context:
In Domain → Information the Neo4j Connection dropdown stayed empty until the
user clicked the refresh button, so there was usually nothing to pick and the
save either sent an empty name (rejected server-side) or appeared to not
persist. Two causes: `loadNeo4jDatabases()` was only bound to the refresh
button, and the option list captured the target selection *before* its fetch,
so a list refresh could overwrite the value hydrated from `/domain/info`.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js`
   Added `syncNeo4jConnectionSection()` — reveals the selector and populates it
   from `/settings/graph-engine/neo4j-connections`; wired to page init and to
   the Graph Backend `change` event. `_loadNeo4jConnectionOptions()` now reads
   the target selection after the fetch resolves, so a late `/domain/info`
   hydration is preserved. Added an in-flight guard so a single reveal issues
   one request; the refresh button forces a reload.
2. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js`
   Blocks the save with a warning when Graph Backend is Neo4j and no connection
   is selected, and refreshes `data-saved-value` after a successful save so a
   later list refresh re-selects the persisted name.
3. `tests/units/domain/test_domain_neo4j_connection_picker.py`
   New contracts: auto-population, repopulation on backend change, saved value
   read after the fetch, request de-duplication, forced refresh, save guard and
   saved-value baseline update.

